          "responseFile": "/tmp/permitext-fresh-hybrid-development-live-20261002/34478c9d-9972-4bcb-aa12-030eaa270d5b-response.json",
          "responseSHA256": "299071bd246a734a3af5f0a92aa3284e36e30d9c073c5106d68bc0f0befc8912",
          "pass": false,
          "issues": [
            {
              "type": "misstated_provision",
              "detail": "The answer says it is unclear whether ZR § 44-44 applies in C4-2. But the supplied passage identifies the section as applying to “M1 M2 M3”; it does not establish the section’s surfacing requirement for C4-2. The opening “No, if…” also risks applying that requirement to this C4-2 facility. Revise to say that § 44-44 requires dustless hard surfacing for the covered permanent open accessory group parking facilities, but the supplied text does not establish that this rule governs C4-2. Do not infer that bare soil is permitted overall: the supplied evidence does not resolve that question under other potentially applicable rules."
            }
          ],
