          "responseSHA256": "b99085b4540c9f4f48f2e84260e7ca7a3791918085c9e73032647d4845849c16",
          "writerAnswerText": "**No—not on the facts stated.** For driveways, parking stalls, and open spaces used to park or store motor vehicles, the surface must be concrete, asphalt, or an equivalent durable, dustless material. Dustlessness alone is not enough if the paving is not also durable; but inadequate drainage or water collecting does not, by itself, establish that this surfacing rule is unsatisfied. (BC § 406.9.4)\n\nSeparately, site grading must not cause storm water to flow across sidewalks or onto adjacent property, subject to what the code otherwise permits. The supplied rule does not say that all water must drain away from the site or prohibit water collecting there. (PC § 1101.12)",
