              "type": "missed_material_conclusion",
              "detail": "The opening “No—not on the facts stated” answers that the surfacing rule is not satisfied, but the cited BC § 406.9.4 requires a qualifying surface—concrete, asphalt, or an equivalent durable, dustless material—and does not make adequate site drainage a condition of that surfacing rule. The answer itself later says water collecting does not establish that the surfacing rule is unsatisfied. State instead that drainage alone does not determine compliance; dustlessness is established, but whether the surface meets the rule also depends on its material and durability."
